{% comment %}
Prompt C's user message, in three parts.

The goal as written, one line per step: the step (its comments above it, its indentation kept), then
after `=> decider:` what the decider listed for it (step.Pick.Listed: each action with its score and
mark), then after `=> formal:` the starting line (step.Pick.Formal) when anything is certain, then
after `=> types:` the variables the step reads whose type the build knows (step.Typed, the walk's).

Types — the literal types first (text, number, bool, list, dict), then every type a listed action's
properties use, in the order the goal first reaches them: the type's Description, a choice's options,
its Example, whichever it has.

Settings — only when a step names a %!path% whose root is a class of settings (step.Setting, the walk's):
each class once, in the order the steps first name it, as %!path%(option: type = default, …).

Keys — only when a step reads one of the app's by its key (%!app.goal["/show"]%, step.HasKey): the one line
that teaches the form.

Then every listed action ONCE (goal.call too when a listed action holds actions): its signature, the
first line of its description, its notes (their headings one level down).

Its shape is pinned by PickListTests (PLang.Tests/Wire/App/Decider/pick_golden.json, the `user` field).
Needs: goal (its steps' Pick taken), modules (%!app.module.list%).
{% endcomment %}Goal, as written:
